    "title": "Snakes and Ladders",
    "category": "Queue",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "problemStatement": "You are given an n \u00d7 n Snakes and Ladders board. Starting from square 1, each move consists of rolling a six-sided die and moving accordingly. If the destination square contains the start of a ladder or the head of a snake, immediately move to its destination. Return the minimum number of moves required to reach the final square. Return -1 if it is impossible.",
    "input": "Integer n An n \u00d7 n board.",
    "output": "A single integer representing the minimum number of moves.",
    "constraints": "2 <= n <= 20"
